 "note": "What a correct census would return for every region on the six trolley photographs, and for the products no region landed on. Written from the committed per-region labels in still-labels.json and query-labels.json plus the item lists in counts.json, not invented here.",
 "why": "The census is built and has never executed: it needs an OpenAI key. Its two jobs are both measurable without the model. `isProduct` decides whether a region reaches the bag, which is the whole of the over-count on this corpus. `unmarkedItems` and `inViewCounts` carry the products no badge landed on, which is the whole of the under-count. Running the shipped `applyCensus` over marks a correct model would produce measures the pipeline around the model, and puts a number on what the key is worth.",
